title: Palo Alto Networks: Configuration capacity
agents: paloalto_api
catalog: hw/network/paloalto
license: GPLv2
distribution: checkmk-paloalto-api
description:
 Counts configured objects in the running configuration (all virtual systems,
 shared objects and Panorama pushed rules): security rules, NAT rules, NAT
 rules with dynamic IP and port translation, address objects and groups,
 service objects and groups, zones and virtual systems. Each count is compared
 to the limit the firewall reports for its model ("show system state filter
 cfg.general.max-*"). Default levels are 80/90 percent of the limit. If the device does
 not report a limit for an object type, the limit can be set in the rule
 "Palo Alto capacity", otherwise only the absolute count is shown.

item:
 The object type, e.g. "Security rules", "NAT rules", "Address objects"
 or "Zones".

discovery:
 One service is created per object type the agent was able to count.
